  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "selector",
      "note": "The committed render declares `device.selector_type: LinearServoSelector` (the same on `[mmu_unit unit0]`), with ERCF's real selector hardware coupled to it: `selector_stepper: unit0_selector`, `selector_servo: unit0_selector_servo`, `encoder: unit0`, plus 2.0's per-gate entry sensors (`mmu_entry_switch_pin_0..7` on `^unit0:PC6/PA8/PB11/PB2/PB0/PC4/PC5/PB1`). That is what Happy Hare's family Kconfig specifies -- `if MMU_FAMILY_ERCF` does `imply LINEAR_SERVO_SELECTOR` and `select MMU_HAS_ENCODER` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:6-8) -- and the version choice is nested under that family, so this dossier is traced with `MMU_FAMILY_ERCF` + `MMU_TYPE_ERCF_2_0` (plus the MMB 2.0 shared-exit symbols). A bare `MMU_TYPE_ERCF_2_0` without the family renders Happy Hare's 'Safety' VirtualSelector instead. Rendered selector motion: `selector_move_speed: 200`, `selector_homing_speed: 60`, `selector_accel: 1200`, `servo_buzz_gear_on_down: 3`, `servo_move_angle: 50`. klipper-mmu drives it as a LINEAR selector with a grip servo (`KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_KIND_LINEAR`, `KLIPPER_MMU_SELECTOR_LINEAR_HAS_SERVO`): the carriage homes to its endstop before the first selection and after a fault, moves at the same 200 mm/s (60 mm/s homing, 1200 mm/s^2), and the servo grips at 100 degrees, releases at 30 and travels at 50, driven by Klipper's scheduled software PWM on any GPIO (`KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_SERVO`). Gate positions start from an estimate computed from Happy Hare's CAD geometry (`4.0,27.0,50.0,73.0,96.0,119.0,142.0,165.0` mm) until `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE_SELECTOR` measures the real ones. ERCF 2.0's Thumper Blocks option is offered in menuconfig (`KLIPPER_MMU_ERCF_THUMPER_BLOCKS`). Software candidate: it builds and passes the simulators, but has not run on real hardware."
    },
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "LOAD does not complete in this harness. The render configures the real encoder homing (`extruder_homing_endstop: encoder`, `gate_homing_endstop: encoder`, `gate_endstop_to_encoder: 10`, `encoder_move_validation: 1`, `bowden_allowable_encoder_delta: 20.0`, `skip_cal_encoder: 0`), and the operation records `operations.load.end.tip = 817.046000`, `filament_pos: 4`, `gate_status: 1` with one error: 'Failed to reach extruder encoder endstop after moving 112.5mm'. UNLOAD and EJECT carry the same recorded error. That is the harness's encoder collision-homing loop failing, not an ERCF behaviour: controlled probes put the cause on the encoder choice alone -- this same 2.0 symbol set with a TCRT5000 encoder completes LOAD/UNLOAD/EJECT, on either board -- while the shipped encoder is Binky-8 (1.469 mm/count), for which the loop steps 4.5 mm (3.0 x ceil(1.469 x 10)/10) and never accumulates the delta it requires. The real encoder is kept as shipped; overriding it to make the harness pass would falsify the hardware."
    },
    {
      "concept": "encoder",
      "note": "An encoder is bound (`encoder: unit0`) and its checks are on: `encoder_move_validation: 1`, `bowden_allowable_encoder_delta: 20.0`, `skip_cal_encoder: 0`, `gate_endstop_to_encoder: 10`, with both `gate_homing_endstop` and `extruder_homing_endstop` set to `encoder`. The render does not name the physical part; ERCF 2.0's Kconfig default is a Binky-8 (1.469 mm/count, installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:224-231), and that resolution is what the harness's collision homing cannot converge on: the recorded failure is 112.5 mm of step travel, i.e. 25 x 4.5 mm, where the step is 3.0 x ceil(1.469 x 10)/10. The same symbol set with a finer count (TCRT5000) completes. klipper-mmu turns its encoder input on by default for every ERCF (`KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER`, because Happy Hare's ERCF family selects MMU_HAS_ENCODER): a one-wire click counter on `KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_ENCODER_A`, which needs that pin and `KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER_PULL` set before the image starts. It is used for clog detection (no click over `KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER_DETECTION_LENGTH_MM`, 10 mm, of gear travel), for progress checks during an operation, and to measure the Bowden length with `KLIPPER_MMU_CALIBRATE` when a toolhead switch is fitted. Happy Hare's encoder homing (`gate_homing_endstop: encoder`) is not a klipper-mmu mode: LOAD ends at a local toolhead switch or at FPS arrival."
    },
    {
      "concept": "buffer_type",
      "note": "No `[mmu_buffer unit0]` renders and no buffer key appears anywhere in the dossier, although the family Kconfig implies `MMU_HAS_FILAMENT_BUFFER` (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:9); 2.0's kit does include a filament buffer, but this render supplies no buffer pins or parameters. klipper-mmu has no 'no buffer' build: every image follows the extruder from a buffer input -- a switched pair (`KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_BUFFER_A/B`), a single tension switch (`KLIPPER_MMU_BUFFER_SINGLE_SWITCH`) or the analog DiffA/DiffB pair, so an ERCF build needs a sensored sync-feedback buffer fitted and wired; the loose-filament buffer Happy Hare's `MMU_HAS_FILAMENT_BUFFER` describes has no sensor and does not count."
    },
    {
      "concept": "preload_park",
      "note": "PRELOAD ends at `operations.preload.end.tip = 6.717000` with `gate_preload_parking_distance: -13` and an empty `gate_preload_endstop`, and SELECT leaves the filament there (`operations.select.end.tip = 6.717000`). The -13 is ERCF 2.0's own default (-11 with Thumper blocks, installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.ercf:220-222)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "unload_park",
      "note": "UNLOAD re-homes to the same park: `operations.unload.end.tip = 7.577000` with `gate_parking_distance: -13`, `filament_pos: 0`, `gate_status: 2`; its recorded error is the same 'Failed to reach extruder encoder endstop after moving 112.5mm'. 2.0's -13 is the version's own value (-11 with Thumper blocks, Kconfig.ercf:220-222); 1.1 parks -23 and 3.0 -16 (Kconfig.ercf:264)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "eject_extra",
      "note": "EJECT adds a flat `gate_final_eject_distance: 20` mm past the park, ending at `operations.eject.end.tip = -12.423000` with the only populated end-stop read-out on this device (`end.sensor: mmu_entry`, `end.offset: 137.577`), `filament_pos: 0`, `gate_status: 0`, and the same cumulative 112.5 mm error."
    },
    {
      "concept": "version_diff",
      "note": "The three versions are no longer identical renders, and their recorded behaviour differs. This one (2.0): 8 gates, `show_bypass: 1`, `gear_ratio: 80:20` -> `steps_per_mm: 563.090637` (the same as 1.1), `servo_move_angle: 50`, parking -13, `gate_autoload: 1`, per-gate `mmu_entry_switch_pin_0..7`, end tips 6.717/7.577/-12.423, and LOAD/UNLOAD/EJECT each recording the 112.5 mm encoder-homing error. 1.1: 9 gates, `show_bypass: 0`, `servo_move_angle: 30`, parking -23, no `gate_autoload`, no per-gate entry sensor, the same `steps_per_mm: 563.090637`, end tips -2.883/-2.648/-22.648, and all five operations error-free. 3.0: 8 gates like 2.0 but `gear_ratio: 1:1` -> `steps_per_mm: 140.772659`, parking -16, end tips 4.210/4.121/-15.879, and the same error at 117.0mm. Encoder defaults by version: TCRT5000 / Binky-8 / Binky-12 (Kconfig.ercf:180-186, :224-231, :267-274), which is exactly the axis the harness failure follows: 1.1 with Binky-8 fails identically at 112.5 mm and 2.0/3.0 with TCRT5000 complete, on either board (EASY_BRD_RP2040 or MMB_2_0). v3.0's optional Jack Rabbit mod renders a plain `LinearSelector` (no servo) and sets `filament_always_gripped` (Kconfig.ercf:98-105); it is not selected here."
    }
  ]
}
